    "supported_statement": "A reproducible exploratory P/U ranking run with a few conditional training-family associations; no universal pairing law or superconductivity probability is established.",
    "reasons": [
      "The only raw R1 terms passing the declared three-training-family stability rule are different in two leave-one-family-out fits; the other two fits have none. No raw term is common to all four outer fits.",
      "The single R2 stable PC term belongs only to its own outer-training PCA basis. PC names cannot be compared or combined across folds.",
      "Stability fixes the outer training basis and chosen alpha; it neither refits preprocessing nor adjusts for all searched terms, and is not a causal or FDR guarantee.",
      "The three-training-family criterion is same-sign single-family heads plus pooled training-system bootstrap stability; it is not a separate 64-bootstrap stability demonstration in every family.",
      "The stable-only terms are not a separately fitted or held-family-validated predictor; full-model scores cannot validate each individual stable term.",
      "Tetrahedrality is defined in 148 of 615 raw structures, but both columns are dropped before every outer fit because training coverage is below 50%. This run cannot establish that tetrahedral coordination is irrelevant.",
      "Original MP parent geometry and categorical DFT flags omit carrier filling, correlations, disorder, electronic coupling and measured tuning paths; U remains absence of a positive record, not a measured nonsuperconductor.",
      "These four families and their literature were already inspected; research ascertainment and composition-correlated geometric proxies remain confounders."
